!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-sibling-reference-as-an-array-element-type-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.3 (inline types, proposed for Revision 40)"
  description: """
    A sibling reference stands only at a record field's type. In sugar it parses wherever a reference does, written with
    the whitespace its `!` needs, and desugaring refuses it anywhere else: `[ kind! ]` resolves in place to an array
    construction, and its slot, an array's `element_type`, is a `meta.type_expr`, which has no sibling form, so `kind!`
    is refused where it is written even though `cell` declares `kind`.
    """
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
